# Worklog automation

When `ai_worklog/` exists in the project:

## After meaningful work

Update today's log per `ai_toolkit/workflows/worklog/update-worklog.md`:

- `ai_worklog/daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — **Done**, **TODO**, **Blockers**, **Summary**
- `ai_worklog/TODOS.md` — add, update, or close global TODOs

Required after **make-plan**, **implement-phase**, bugfixes, refactors, and multi-file implementation — not after read-only Q&A.

## Language

- Write all **stored** worklog content in **English**.
- Translate user descriptions (including Arabic) into clear English before saving.
- Generate **Arabic reports** only when the user explicitly asks. Do not rewrite stored files in Arabic.

## Reports

| User says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| `generate today report` | English report in chat only |
| `generate today report in Arabic` | Arabic report in chat only |
| `… and save it` / `export` / `store` | Also write `ai_worklog/reports/YYYY-MM-DD-<en\|ar>.md` |

Follow `ai_toolkit/workflows/worklog/daily-report.md` for structure (Slack-ready sections). Reports must include **Tomorrow** / **ما سيتم العمل عليه غدًا**; if the user attaches tomorrow's plan in the command, include it there.

## TODO IDs

Use `TODO-YYYY-MM-DD-###` (sequential per day). Mirror open items in `TODOS.md` under the correct owner section.

## Before ending a coding session

If work was completed and the worklog was not updated, update it before finishing.
